Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Platform/CIX/Sky1: PcieMenu: manual ASPM selection, x4-wired
 Port0

CIX 2026Q3 reduces ASPM to "ASPM configuration" (Disable/Enable, i.e.
max-aspm-support 0 or 2) and hides the per-port ASPM question.  Expose
both as the Minisforum firmware does: "ASPM Max Support" offers
Disable, L0s, L1 and L0sL1, and "ASPM" offers the states that the
maximum allows.  The maximum is the value the OS sees: AcpiSocDxe
publishes it as the root port's max-aspm-support _DSD property, and
the CIX pci-sky1 driver clears L0s (bit 0) and L1 (bit 1) from the
root port's Link Capabilities when they are not set.  The per-port
selection goes into the "aspm" property.

Several boards wire the x8 root port to an x4 M.2 slot.  A board DSC
that defines PCIE_RP0_X4_SLOT in VFRPP_FLAGS gets Port0 titled
"PCI Express X4(Port0)" and no X8 width option.  The 64-bit window
help names Port0 instead of the x8 slot.
